  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-file-explorer-preview-sequence",
      "text": "[中文](README.zh.md) | English\n\nA [DSH Web](https://deepseek.com) plugin that adds a **SeqViz sequence viewer** to [dsh-file-explorer](https://github.com/wolfsonliu/dsh-file-explorer), overriding its plain-text previews for **FASTA**, **GenBank**, **JBEI**, **SnapGene**, and **SBOL** files.\n\nSelect a `.gb` / `.fasta` (or any supported format below) in the file explorer and the preview panel renders an interactive sequence viewer instead of raw text."
    },
    {
      "section": "Screenshots",
      "text": "| Dark theme | Light theme |\n| --- | --- |\n|  |  |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Interactive viewer** built on [`seqviz`](https://github.com/Lattice-Automation/seqviz) (`<SeqViz>`), with parsing by [`seqparse`](https://github.com/Lattice-Automation/seqparse).\n- **Topologies**: circular / linear / both / both-flip.\n- **Feature annotations** with colors, **search** with highlight, **enzyme cut sites**, complement & index toggles, and linear zoom.\n- **Status bar** with the format badge, name, sequence type, and length.\n- **Selectable viewer**: registered as a named **SeqViz** viewer (dsh-file-explorer v0.9.0+), so it appears in the file row's \"Open with…\" menu and the preview-panel switcher — pick it explicitly for ambiguous `.xml`/`.seq` files, or fall back to plain text.\n- **Localized** toolbar/status copy (中文 / English).\n- **Dark/light aware**: follows DSH's `data-ds-dark-theme`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Supported formats",
      "text": "| Extension | Format |\n|-----------|--------|\n| `fasta` `fa` `fas` `fna` `faa` `ffn` | FASTA |\n| `gb` `gbk` `genbank` `gp` | GenBank / GenPept |\n| `dna` | SnapGene |\n| `seq` | JBEI SEQ |\n| `sbol` `xml` | SBOL v1/v2 |"
    },
    {
      "section": "From the Git repository",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:wolfsonliu/dsh-file-explorer-preview-sequence\ndsh web\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "From source",
      "text": "```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/wolfsonliu/dsh-file-explorer-preview-sequence\ncd dsh-file-explorer-preview-sequence\nnpm install\nnpm run build"
    },
    {
      "section": "Dependencies",
      "text": "This plugin **requires** [`@dsh-external/dsh-file-explorer`](https://github.com/wolfsonliu/dsh-file-explorer) (v0.1.0+) — it injects the `fileExplorer` cordis service (`registerViewer` / `registerPreview` / `writeFile` / `readRawFile`). Install and enable `dsh-file-explorer` before this plugin:\n\n```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "install the core from git",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add github:wolfsonliu/dsh-file-explorer"
    },
    {
      "section": "or, from source",
      "text": "git clone https://github.com/wolfsonliu/dsh-file-explorer\ncd dsh-file-explorer\nnpm install && npm run build\ndsh plugin --profile web add .\n```\n\n> For local development, this repo's `devDependencies` resolves `@dsh-external/dsh-file-explorer`'s `./client` type definitions. Point it at your checkout or your registry's published package before `npm install`."
    },
    {
      "section": "or, from source",
      "text": "For files ≤ 2 MiB the plugin parses the `text` preview content directly. SnapGene `.dna` (binary) and files larger than 2 MiB are handled via `readRawFile` (available in dsh-file-explorer v0.1.0+). When `readRawFile` is absent (older core versions), the plugin degrades gracefully: text formats ≤ 2 MiB still preview, `.dna` and larger files show an unsupported status."
    },
    {
      "section": "or, from source",
      "text": "On dsh-file-explorer v0.9.0+ the plugin also registers via `registerViewer`, giving it a single named **SeqViz** entry in \"Open with…\"; on older cores it falls back to per-extension `registerPreview` registrations."
    },
    {
      "section": "Limitations",
      "text": "- Read-only preview (no editing).\n- SnapGene `.dna` and > 2 MiB files require dsh-file-explorer v0.1.0+ (older versions degrade gracefully).\n- `.xml` and `.seq` are ambiguous extensions; files in those extensions that aren't SBOL / JBEI fall back to a plain-text view."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm run check   # tsc type check\nnpm test        # vitest unit tests\nnpm run build   # tsc + tsdown (single-file lib/client.js bundling seqviz + seqparse)\n```\n\nThe real SeqViz canvas cannot run under jsdom; verify it with `dsh web` and a sequence file in `examples/`.\n\n> After `npm run build`, hard-refresh the browser (`Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+R`): `dsh web` may keep serving a cached plugin bundle, so a soft reload can leave your latest build unused."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE)"
    }
  ],
